# `for (const [key, count] of counts.entries())` walks the table of the map in line, and the key and the value go from the entries straight into the multiplication.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="total" role=Source
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[table]] = Load(b@[[map]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Reads:CollectionStorage, {{*}}:CollectionTable)
# CHECK: Patchpoint({{*}}isLoopPoll{{*}}:LoopHint)
# CHECK: Load(b@{{*}}Reads:CollectionEntries, {{*}}:MapNext)
# CHECK: Double b@[[product]] = Mul(b@{{*}}, b@{{*}}, {{*}}:Mul)
# CHECK: Double b@{{*}} = Add(b@{{*}}, b@[[product]], {{*}}:Add)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# The pair of key and value is never made, so nothing reads an element of an array.
# NONE-LABEL: name="total" role=Source
# NONE-NOT: :NewArray)
# NONE-NOT: :GetArrayElement)
# NONE-NOT: Reads:JSObject_butterfly
# NONE-LABEL: end of function
# The one patchpoint on the likely paths is the poll.
# The function has calls, and Windows passes arguments in other registers: its count is not checked.
# X64: instructions: 74, patchpoints: 1, rare instructions: 11
# ARM64: instructions: 87, patchpoints: 1, rare instructions: 13
